// `#[column]`'s arguments are **named**, and a wrong one is refused rather than ignored.
//
// Named rather than positional was the decision: `#[column("start_date")]` reads fine today and
// stops reading the moment a second argument exists -- which is a when rather than an if, since
// `required:` was asked for alongside `name:` and was left out only because nothing reads it yet.
// A misspelled argument is the case that matters most: ignored, it would be a column override
// that silently does not happen.
struct E {
    #[column(nmae: "x")]
    a: int
}

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
